      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The North Pacific Coast Railroad began stopping in Valley Ford in 1876, linking ranchers and fishers to San Francisco and boosting local trade.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valley_Ford%2C_California",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Watson School served Valley Ford from 1856 to 1967; today it sits in a historic park 3.5 miles north of town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
